request.description:
## Apply Loyalty Points

Applies a customer's loyalty points as a discount to their Shopify cart. This endpoint generates a Shopify discount code equivalent to the points value and returns it for use at checkout.

The `data` parameter must be the Base64-encoded response from Shopify's `/cart.js` endpoint for the customer's current cart. The `spent_rule_id` identifies which redemption rule to apply — retrieve valid rule IDs from the [Get Customer Available Spent Rule](#get-customer-available-spent-rule) API.

**Request Parameters:**

| Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
|-----------|------|----------|-------------|
| `data` | string | Yes | Base64-encoded response from Shopify `/cart.js` for the customer's current cart |
| `spent_rule_id` | integer | Yes | Loyalty points redemption rule ID to apply. Retrieve from [Get Customer Available Spent Rule](#get-customer-available-spent-rule). **Example: `5`** |

> **Note:** For most stores, the loyalty points redemption rule ID is typically `5`, but merchants should always fetch the available value using the [Get Customer Available Spent Rule](#get-customer-available-spent-rule) API.
---

### Code Samples

#### cURL

```bash
# 1. Get cart data from Shopify and Base64-encode it
CART_DATA=$(curl -s "https://your-store.myshopify.com/cart.js" | base64)

# 2. Apply loyalty points
curl --location 'https://app.getflits.com/api/1/{{storeID}}/{{customerID}}/credit/apply_credit?token={{flits_token}}' \
  --header 'Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded' \
  --data-urlencode "data=$CART_DATA" \
  --data-urlencode 'spent_rule_id=5'
```

#### JavaScript (Fetch)

```js
const storeID    = process.env.STORE_ID;
const customerID = process.env.CUSTOMER_ID;
const token      = process.env.FLITS_TOKEN;

// 1. Get cart data from Shopify and Base64-encode it
const cartRes  = await fetch('/cart.js');
const cartJson = await cartRes.text();
const cartData = btoa(cartJson);

// 2. Apply loyalty points
const url  = `https://app.getflits.com/api/1/${storeID}/${customerID}/credit/apply_credit?token=${token}`;
const body = new URLSearchParams({ data: cartData, spent_rule_id: '5' });

const res = await fetch(url, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/x-www-form-urlencoded' },
  body,
});
console.log(await res.json());
```

#### Python (requests)

```python
import os, base64, requests

store_id    = os.environ.get('STORE_ID')
customer_id = os.environ.get('CUSTOMER_ID')
token       = os.environ.get('FLITS_TOKEN')

# 1. Get cart data from Shopify and Base64-encode it
cart_res  = requests.get('https://your-store.myshopify.com/cart.js')
cart_data = base64.b64encode(cart_res.content).decode()

# 2. Apply loyalty points
url    = f"https://app.getflits.com/api/1/{store_id}/{customer_id}/credit/apply_credit"
params = {'token': token}
data   = {'data': cart_data, 'spent_rule_id': 5}

response = requests.post(url, params=params, data=data)
print(response.json())
```

#### PHP (cURL)

```php
$storeID    = getenv('STORE_ID');
$customerID = getenv('CUSTOMER_ID');
$token      = getenv('FLITS_TOKEN');

// 1. Get cart data from Shopify and Base64-encode it
$cartJson = file_get_contents('https://your-store.myshopify.com/cart.js');
$cartData = base64_encode($cartJson);

// 2. Apply loyalty points
$url = "https://app.getflits.com/api/1/{$storeID}/{$customerID}/credit/apply_credit?token={$token}";

$ch = curl_init($url);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_RETURNTRANSFER, true);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POST, true);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_HTTPHEADER, ['Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded']);
curl_setopt($ch, CURLOPT_POSTFIELDS, http_build_query([
    'data'          => $cartData,
    'spent_rule_id' => 5,
]));

$response = curl_exec($ch);
curl_close($ch);
$result = json_decode($response, true);
print_r($result);
```

#### HTTP

```http
POST /api/1/{{storeID}}/{{customerID}}/credit/apply_credit?token={{flits_token}} HTTP/1.1
Host: app.getflits.com
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

data={{cart_data_base64}}&spent_rule_id=5
```

---

### Response Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `status` | boolean | `true` on success, `false` on error |
| `code` | string | Shopify discount code to apply at checkout (present when `status: true`) |
| `cart_value_to_apply_credit` | number | Cart value used to calculate the discount, returned in a **100× multiplied format** — divide by 100 to get the actual amount (e.g. `257400 → 2574`). Present when `status: true`. |
| `customer_email` | string | Customer email address (present when `status: true`) |
| `LOYALTY_POINTS_DISCOUNT_CODE_PREFIX` | string | Prefix used for loyalty points discount codes (present when `status: true`) |
| `STORE_CREDIT_DISCOUNT_CODE_PREFIX` | string | Prefix used for store credit discount codes (present when `status: true`) |
| `error` | string | Error message (present when `status: false`) |

> **Note:** `cart_value_to_apply_credit` is returned in a **100× multiplied format**. Divide by 100 to get the original currency amount.
>
> Example: `257400 → 2574`

> **All business logic errors return HTTP 200** — always check `status` in the response body, not the HTTP status code alone.

